{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Xo7w2Vz5wg8n1cudwuvMDv","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# crc8\n2\t\n3\tByte-wise CRC-8 engine (CRC-8/SMBUS parameters).\n4\t\n5\t## Parameters of the CRC\n6\t- Polynomial: x^8 + x^2 + x + 1 (`0x07`, normal/MSB-first form)\n7\t- Initial value: `0x00`\n8\t- No input or output reflection, no final XOR.\n9\t- Check value: the CRC of the ASCII string `\"123456789\"` (bytes 0x31..0x39) is `0xF4`.\n10\t\n11\t## Ports\n12\t| Port  | Dir | Width | Description |\n13\t|-------|-----|-------|-------------|\n14\t| clk   | in  | 1     | Rising-edge clock |\n15\t| rst_n | in  | 1     | Asynchronous active-low reset |\n16\t| clear | in  | 1     | Synchronous clear of the running CRC |\n17\t| valid | in  | 1     | `data` holds a byte to be absorbed this cycle |\n18\t| data  | in  | 8     | Input byte |\n19\t| crc   | out | 8     | Running CRC register |\n20\t\n21\t## Behavior\n22\t- While `rst_n` is low, `crc` is `0x00`.\n23\t- On each rising edge of `clk`:\n24\t  - if `clear` is 1, `crc` becomes `0x00`. `clear` has priority: if `valid` is also 1 in that\n25\t    cycle, the byte on `data` is discarded (not absorbed).\n26\t  - else if `valid` is 1, `crc` becomes the CRC update of the old `crc` with the full 8-bit byte,\n27\t    processed MSB first: `x = crc ^ data`, then repeat 8 times:\n28\t    `x = x[7] ? ((x << 1) ^ 8'h07) : (x << 1)` (8-bit arithmetic); the result is the new `crc`.\n29\t  - otherwise `crc` holds.\n30\t- `crc` therefore always equals the CRC-8 of all bytes absorbed since the last reset/clear.\n31\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8c036b0c-3d09-4fa0-a3d1-ee30e05a3aed","uuid":"f0095bd8-906b-4c86-a008-a9653123b8af","timestamp":"2026-10-19T23:48:32.452Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\abhig\\Documents\\New folder\\assay\\runs\\v1__crc8__t2\\workspace\\spec.md","content":"# crc8\n\nByte-wise CRC-8 engine (CRC-8/SMBUS parameters).\n\n## Parameters of the CRC\n- Polynomial: x^8 + x^2 + x + 1 (`0x07`, normal/MSB-first form)\n- Initial value: `0x00`\n- No input or output reflection, no final XOR.\n- Check value: the CRC of the ASCII string `\"123456789\"` (bytes 0x31..0x39) is `0xF4`.\n\n## Ports\n| Port  | Dir | Width | Description |\n|-------|-----|-------|-------------|\n| clk   | in  | 1     | Rising-edge clock |\n| rst_n | in  | 1     | Asynchronous active-low reset |\n| clear | in  | 1     | Synchronous clear of the running CRC |\n| valid | in  | 1     | `data` holds a byte to be absorbed this cycle |\n| data  | in  | 8     | Input byte |\n| crc   | out | 8     | Running CRC register |\n\n## Behavior\n- While `rst_n` is low, `crc` is `0x00`.\n- On each rising edge of `clk`:\n  - if `clear` is 1, `crc` becomes `0x00`. `clear` has priority: if `valid` is also 1 in that\n    cycle, the byte on `data` is discarded (not absorbed).\n  - else if `valid` is 1, `crc` becomes the CRC update of the old `crc` with the full 8-bit byte,\n    processed MSB first: `x = crc ^ data`, then repeat 8 times:\n    `x = x[7] ? ((x << 1) ^ 8'h07) : (x << 1)` (8-bit arithmetic); the result is the new `crc`.\n  - otherwise `crc` holds.\n- `crc` therefore always equals the CRC-8 of all bytes absorbed since the last reset/clear.\n","numLines":31,"startLine":1,"totalLines":31}}}
